# API Key Management Service — REST API Design

Base path: `/v1`

## 1. Endpoints

| Method | Path | JWT scope | Success | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/v1/keys` | `keys:write` | `201` | Create a key. Full secret returned **once**. |
| `GET` | `/v1/keys` | `keys:read` | `200` | List keys (metadata + prefix only). |
| `DELETE` | `/v1/keys/:id` | `keys:write` | `200` | Revoke a key (sets `revokedAt`). |
| `POST` | `/v1/keys/:id/rotate` | `keys:write` | `201` | Atomically revoke + reissue under the same name. |

Revoke is `DELETE`, not `POST /keys/:id/revoke` — revocation is exactly the state transition `DELETE` expresses (the row remains for audit, but the credential is dead). There is no `POST /keys/:id/revoke` route.

